{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Let Adonai go among us.</b> As You promised — since You bear iniquity. And if they are a stiff-necked people and they rebel against You, and You said on this account ״lest I consume you on the way״ — You will pardon our iniquity, and so on. The כִּי is in place of אִם." "<b>And our heritage.</b> And make us a heritage uniquely Yours — this is the request of ״and we shall be distinguished, I and Your people״ — that Your Presence not rest upon the nations."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:29.817767674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}